Day 70 – Variables, Facts, Conditionals and Loops

Today I learned how to make Ansible Playbooks more flexible using basic Variables, Facts, Conditionals and Loops.

What I Learned

1. Variables

Variables store reusable values.

Example:

vars:
  app_name: my-app
  app_port: 8080

Using variables:

{{ app_name }}
{{ app_port }}

2. Ansible Facts

Ansible automatically collects system information from managed hosts.

I practiced getting:

- Hostname
- Operating System
- RAM
- IP Address

Example:

{{ ansible_hostname }}
{{ ansible_distribution }}
{{ ansible_memtotal_mb }}
{{ ansible_default_ipv4.address }}

3. Conditionals

The "when" condition allows a task to run only when a condition is true.

Example:

- name: Check Ubuntu
  debug:
    msg: "This is an Ubuntu server"
  when: ansible_distribution == "Ubuntu"

4. Loops

Loops allow one task to work with multiple values.

Example:

loop:
  - /tmp/app
  - /tmp/logs
  - /tmp/config

I used a loop to create multiple directories.

